 ## Overview
-Volumetric isosurface rendering with intersection refinement is a real-time technique that extracts an isosurface directly from a 3D volumetric scalar field during ray traversal, avoiding explicit polygon mesh extraction (e.g., Marching Cubes) [S1, S3]. It detects the surface by finding intervals where the scalar field changes sign relative to an isovalue and refines the intersection position to reduce discretization artifacts [S3]. Unlike [Differentiable Volumetric Rendering (DVR)](775-differentiable-volumetric-rendering-dvr.md), which composites the entire volume, this method stops at the first hit, offering higher performance for opaque surfaces [S3]. It differs from [Real-Time Ray-Casting and Advanced Shading of Discrete Isosurfaces](838-real-time-ray-casting-and-advanced-shading-of-discrete-isosu.md) by operating on implicit continuous data rather than discrete extracted meshes [S3].
+Volumetric isosurface rendering with intersection refinement is a real-time technique that extracts an isosurface directly from a 3D volumetric scalar field during ray traversal, avoiding explicit polygon mesh extraction (e.g., Marching Cubes) [S1, S3]. It detects the surface by finding intervals where the scalar field changes sign relative to an isovalue [S1], or stops when the sampled value exceeds the isovalue [S3], and refines the intersection position to reduce discretization artifacts [S3]. Unlike [Differentiable Volumetric Rendering (DVR)](775-differentiable-volumetric-rendering-dvr.md), which composites the entire volume, this method stops at the first hit, offering higher performance for opaque surfaces [S3]. It differs from [Real-Time Ray-Casting and Advanced Shading of Discrete Isosurfaces](838-real-time-ray-casting-and-advanced-shading-of-discrete-isosu.md) by operating on implicit continuous data rather than discrete extracted meshes [S3].
 
