 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of samples along the ray. The cost is dominated by texture lookups. Refinement adds a constant factor ($k$ iterations) only when a hit is found. Shadow rays add another traversal pass.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Low. Requires storage for the 3D volume texture and small UBOs. No explicit mesh geometry is stored [S1, S3].
-*   **Performance:** Real-time on modern GPUs [S1]. Performance scales with resolution and step size. Smaller step sizes increase accuracy but reduce frame rate [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of samples along the ray [S1]. The cost is dominated by texture lookups [S2]. Refinement adds a constant factor ($k$ iterations) only when a hit is found [S1]. Shadow rays add another traversal pass [S1].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Low [S1]. Requires storage for the 3D volume texture and small UBOs [S1]. No explicit mesh geometry is stored [S1, S3].
+*   **Performance:** Real-time on modern GPUs [S1]. Performance scales with resolution and step size [S1]. Smaller step sizes increase accuracy but reduce frame rate [S1].
 *   **Optimizations:**
     *   **Empty-space skipping:** Using a 32x32x32 brick min/max acceleration structure allows rays to jump over regions that cannot contain the isovalue [S2].
